[ti:Analog Veins]
[00:27.88][Verse]
[00:27.96]Red heels on the wet concrete
[00:30.00]Dial tone ringing on a vacant street
[00:32.16]Half a glass of bourbon by the old TV
[00:34.48]Static on the screen, just you and me
[00:37.76]Elevator hums to the fourteenth floor
[00:39.04]Slide the plastic card into a heavy door
[00:41.16]No one asks your name, no one ever will
[00:43.60]Time is standing still, but we're moving still
[00:45.76]The neon dies but the glow remains
[00:50.00]Running digital blood through analog veins
[00:54.88]The bar won't close, the city won't sleep
[00:58.84]We're drowning in the shallow, sinking in the deep
[01:02.00]Tomorrow never comes, the night just spins
[01:04.56]Another glass, another song, another place begins
[01:18.52][Verse]
[01:18.60]Vending machine flickers in the hall
[01:20.16]Shadows bleeding out across the velvet wall
[01:22.48]Cigarette burns down to the very end
[01:25.04]Don't need a lover, don't want a friend
[01:27.16]Midnight radio playing something slow
[01:30.00]Distant siren wailing, nowhere left to go
[01:31.60]Perfectly numb in a crowded space
[01:33.92]Looking for a feeling in a plastic face
[01:36.04]The neon dies but the glow remains
[01:40.28]Running digital blood through analog veins
[01:45.16]The bar won't close, the city won't sleep
[01:49.16]We're drowning in the shallow, sinking in the deep
[01:52.28]Tomorrow never comes, the night just spins
[01:54.88]Another glass, another song, another place begins
[02:49.08][Bridge]
[02:49.16]Keep the curtains drawn, ignore the sky
[02:51.60]Nothing left to sell, nothing left to buy
[02:53.72]Just the hum of the wire and the heavy air
[02:56.04]I'd leave it all behind, if I even cared
[02:58.52][Chorus]
[02:58.60]The neon dies but the glow remains
[03:02.56]Running digital blood through analog veins
